---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Agent Toolkit — portable capabilities for coding agents"
  description="Discover and distribute portable skills, agents, MCP templates and workflows for AI coding tools. Use Agent Toolkit from the CLI or Veasel Code."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Portable capabilities · CLI and catalog</p>
        <h1>Useful capabilities for the coding agents you already use.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Agent Toolkit brings skills, agent personas, MCP templates, context
          packs and repeatable workflows to your coding tools. Keep your
          capabilities portable; choose the runtime that fits the work.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button" href="/capabilities/">
            Explore capabilities{" "}
            <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          </a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/installation/">
            Install the CLI{" "}
            <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-footnote">
          <strong>One portable toolkit.</strong> Use supported integrations with
          Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, Veasel and other coding agents.
          Support varies by capability and tool.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-grid" aria-label="Portable capability types">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h2>Skills</h2>
          <p>Reusable instructions for focused work.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h2>Agents</h2>
          <p>Personas and role definitions for compatible tools.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h2>MCP</h2>
          <p>Templates to configure external tool connections.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h2>Workflows</h2>
          <p>Repeatable recipes, loops and context packs.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--glow">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="section-kicker">Choose your runtime</p>
        <h2>Portable capabilities. Clear product roles.</h2>
        <p>
          Agent Toolkit is the portable capability layer and CLI. Veasel Code is
          the graphical coding application and shared session runtime. The
          official Veasel catalog curates plugins for that runtime.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="semantic-list">
        <article class="semantic-item">
          <span class="term">PORTABLE TOOLKIT</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Agent Toolkit</strong>
            <br />
            Install and validate capabilities for supported coding tools.
          </p>
          <a href="/docs/installation/">CLI installation guide →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="semantic-item">
          <span class="term">CODING APPLICATION</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Veasel Code</strong>
            <br />
            Use the TUI and Desktop with one canonical backend and shared
            sessions.
          </p>
          <a href="https://www.veasel.dev/downloads/">Get Veasel Code →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="semantic-item">
          <span class="term">GOVERNED CATALOG</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Official Veasel plugins</strong>
            <br />
            Discover curated manifests with provenance and review status.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/agent-toolkit">
            Browse the catalog →
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--deep">
    <div class="wrap closing-banner">
      <p class="section-kicker">Inspect before installing</p>
      <h2>Know what a capability will change.</h2>
      <p>
        Preview install targets, preserve files you own, and inspect provenance
        before applying capabilities. Compatibility depends on the target tool;
        the CLI reports unsupported or unavailable targets instead of guessing.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/installation/">
          Read installation guide
        </a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/compatibility/">
          Check compatibility
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
